      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Both approaches have strengths, as the ideal curriculum depends on your school's goals. A focus on shared values can build community and provide a strong sense of national identity. Conversely, emphasizing systemic injustices fosters critical thinking and helps students understand complex social dynamics relevant to the modern world. Many educators find a balanced approach, weaving both historical successes and critical analyses into the learning structure, which can provide a more complete understanding for students.",
